course: dictionary
lesson: 11700
title: Attired: dressed in a particular way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to formal writing, such as invitations, speeches and old stories. Attired is one of them. It is a formal way of saying dressed.
explain: «The king was attired in a long blue robe with gold thread.» The clues are robe and gold thread, which are clothes, so attired must mean dressed in a particular way.
explain: Attired often comes with a phrase that tells you how someone was dressed, such as smartly attired. «The guests were smartly attired for the wedding.» That means they wore neat, smart clothes.
explain: Use the swap check. Put dressed in place of attired: «The king was dressed in a long blue robe» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Attired means dressed in a particular way.
fact: Attired is a formal word, mostly found in writing and stories.
fact: Attired is an adjective, and it is the past form of the rare verb attire.
fact: «Smartly attired» means dressed neatly and well.
fact: «Suitably attired» means dressed in the right clothes for an occasion.
exercise: «The guests were smartly attired for the wedding.» What does attired mean here? | *Dressed in a particular way | Sent away early | Tired after a long day | Hungry for cake
exercise: «The queen was attired in silk and pearls.» Find and copy the word that tells how the queen was dressed. | *attired | silk | pearls | queen
exercise: Ella says, «The waiter was smartly attired.» What does smartly attired mean? | Covered in mud after football | Hungry and cold | *Dressed neatly and well | Very sleepy
test: «The band was attired in black suits for the concert.» What does attired mean? | Tired and bored | *Dressed in a particular way | Sitting down | Playing very loudly
test: Which phrase means dressed in the right clothes for the event? | *Suitably attired | Famished and cold | Barely attired | Glum and quiet
exam: What does attired mean in «The doctor, attired in a white coat, smiled at the children»? | *Dressed in a particular way | Running fast | Asleep | Sad and quiet
